---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/discount-strategy';
const title = "Set recovery incentives from contribution and eligibility";
const desc = "A discount is a cost with a redemption policy, not a required final step in every recovery sequence. Start with the problem preventing purchase and the contribution available to fund an offer.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/use-cases" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All use cases</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-slate-700">{desc}</p>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-12">
      <h2>Define the economic boundary</h2>
      <p>Calculate contribution after the actual discount, product costs, payment fees, fulfillment, shipping subsidy and expected returns. A percentage discount reduces selling revenue; it is not merely that percentage of gross profit. Use the specific basket and destination instead of a reference average order value to authorize an incentive.</p>
      <h2>Separate help from subsidy</h2>
      <p>If the obstacle is sizing, delivery eligibility or a failed payment, an offer may leave it unresolved. Try the relevant information or support route first. Compare an incentive branch with a no-incentive branch among otherwise eligible customers; do not infer discount sensitivity solely from prior redemptions.</p>
      <h2>Specify redemption behavior</h2>
      <p>Document eligible products, minimum spend, expiry timezone, usage limits and combination rules. Decide whether codes are customer-bound and what happens if a shopper changes the basket or forwards the email. Test the actual checkout combination rather than writing “cannot stack” while another promotion remains combinable.</p>
      <h2>Control competing promises</h2>
      <p>Use one offer owner across cart recovery, winback and public campaigns. Recent discount use and full-price purchase history may inform a policy but are not automatic exclusions for every store. Route price fairness questions to an explicit support policy, and keep eligibility explanations consistent between email and checkout.</p>
      <h2>Proposed decision review</h2>
      <p>Inspect a mixed-margin basket, a partial return and a code redeemed outside the recovery link. Compare net contribution per assigned eligible customer, code leakage and support contacts. Increase subsidy only when the evidence supports it; attributed discounted orders alone do not reveal whether the incentive caused the sale.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
